    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d983">

                <pb facs="1038" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/3401</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hale</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-07T20:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1916, 8 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 8, 7.30 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Costa Rican Minister for Foreign Affairs has called to ask advice as follows:</p>
                <p>He says that the Italian Minister two weeks ago telegraphed to know if the Costa
                    Rican Government would admit into its ports an Italian [merchant<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d983-f1"/>] vessel “armed against submarines.” He replied, “No.” He
                    received to-day another telegram from the Italian Minister saying that the
                    United States had granted a similar request. He says that the Costa Rican
                    Government desires to conform to the policy of the United States and that he
                    asks advice in the present case. Please instruct me by cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hale</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d983-f1" n="2" xml:id="d983-f1-content">
